# RULE (CLAUDE.md, "A LINK THAT DROPS OVER A LOG ALREADY FETCHED"):
#   A reconnect is held until it has bytes, and the guard sits BEFORE refreshSize() —
#   that call is what ADOPTS the new generation, and once it has, the index's offsets
#   name bytes the new spool file does not hold.
#
# GUARD: tst_waitingremote::aHeldReconnectLeavesTheCachedRecordsReadableAndNotMerelyCounted
#
# SILENT WHEN BROKEN: the ROW COUNT is what survives the mistake, so the table still
# looks right — every record decodes to nothing, with no way back for the life of the
# tab. tst_waitingremote::aReconnectHoldsTheCachedRecordsUntilItsFirstBytes asserts the
# count and passes throughout, which is why the guard reads the cells.

